      "textEn": "Shri-Shuka said—Shri Shukadeva Goswami said; Atra—in the Srimad Bhagavatam; Anuvarnyate—is described in detail;\nAbhikshnam—again and again; Vishwa-Atma—the soul of the entire universe; Bhagavan—God; Harih—Hari; Yasya—of whom;\nPrasad—by being pleased; Jah—produced; Brahma—Brahma; Rudrah—Shiva; Krodha—from anger; Samudbhavah—produced. Shukdev Goswami said: In the various stories of this Shrimad Bhagwat, Lord Hari's\ndetailed description has been given, by whose pleasure Brahmaji is born, and by whose anger\nRudra is born. Meaning: Srila Vishwanath Chakravarti Thakur, while commenting on this verse, has presented a detailed summary of Srimad Bhagavatam. The essence of this great Acharya's statement is that Shukdev Goswami\nhas described the self-willed, loving dedication towards Lord Krishna, which is the highest\nachievement of life. The sole purpose of Shrimad Bhagwat is to assure the bound soul for such a dedication to God,\nand to go to the abode of God.\nYou, O King, will kill this animal-like intellect. You are not going to be born, you are already born, you are not going to be born. 2. Meaning of the word\n\nTvam—you; Tu—but; Rajan—Oh king; Marishye—I am going to die; Iti—Thinking this; Pashu-buddhim—of an animalistic\nmindset; Imam—This; Jahi—give up; Na—not; Jatah—born; Prak—before this; Abhuutah—unborn; Adya—today; Deha-vat—like the body; Tvam—you; Na—not; Nadakshyasi—will not be destroyed. Oh King, abandon your brutal tendency to think, \"I'm gonna die\". You\nare completely different from the body because you have not taken birth. There was no such time in the past\nwhen you were not, and you are not going to be destroyed either. Meaning: In the end of the first book (1.19.15), King Parikshit had said—\n\nTam mopajatam pratiniyantu vipra Ganga cha devi dhrita-chittamisha.\nDvijopasrishta, Kuhakastakshako, or Dashatvalam, these Vishnu stories are sung. \"Here, Brahmin! You accept me as a completely surrendered soul, and the mother Ganga, who is the representative of God, accept me in the same form because I have already placed the lotus feet of God in my heart. May any magical object produced by Takshak or a Brahmin come and immediately cut me. My only wish is that you people keep singing the works of Lord Vishnu.\nKeep singing.\"\n\nEven before listening to the Shrimad Bhagavat, King Parikshit was a great devotee of the Lord. In the king's mind, there was no\nbrutal fear of death, but Shukdev Goswami is speaking to us in the same way, with sharp words from his disciple, just as Lord Krishna speaks to Arjuna in the Bhagavad Gita in harsh words. Do not be in the future, you are in the form of son, grandson, etc."
