      "textEn": "The mind creates the qualities of the body and the actions of the self. The mind creates illusion, then the life is in the world. 6. Meaning of the word\n\nMind—mind; creates—creates; without—indeed; body—to the physical bodies; qualities—to the qualities; actions—to the actions\nTo; and; of the self—of the self; that—that; mind—mind; creates—creates; illusion—the power of God's illusion;\nTherefore—in this way; of the living being—of the living being; existence—existence..\n\nThe physical body, qualities, and actions of the soul are produced only by the physical mind. Mind\nIt originates from the illusionary power of God himself, and in this way, the soul assumes a physical existence. Snehadhisthanavartyaagnisamyogo yavaddayate. The lamp of the lamp-light, thus the body is made.\nRajas-sattva-tamo-vrittya-jayate atha vinashyati. 7. Meaning of the word:\n\nAffection—of oil; base—of vessel; light—of wick; fire—and fire; union—of confluence; as far as—as far as; seen—seen;\nApparent—apparent; of lamp—of lamp; the state of being as a lamp; likewise—likewise; caused by—caused by; the world—the world; of rajas—of rajas; of sattva—of sattva; of tamas—of tamas; by action—by action; arises—arises; then—then; perishes—perishes. The lamp works only by the combination of its fuel, container, wick and fire. Similarly,\nphysical life arises from being based on the identification of the soul with the body, and\nis destroyed by the actions of the Rajo, Tamo, and Satoguna, which are the constituent elements of the body. There, the self-illuminating, unmanifest and manifest, is beyond.\nThe sky is like a cloud, and the earth is like a mountain, beyond comparison. 8 ”. Meaning of the word\n\nN—No; Tatra—There; Atma—Soul; Swayam-Jyotih—self-illuminated; Yah—He; Vyakta-Avyakta-yoah—manifested and\nUnmanifested (gross and subtle bodies); Parah—Different; Akashah—Sky; Iva—Like; Cha—And; Adharah—Base;\nDhruva—Fixed; Ananta—Infinite; Upamah—Or Comparison; Tatah—Thus. The soul within the body is self-illuminated and separate from the visible gross and invisible subtle bodies. This remains a stable base for changing bodies, just as the sky\nis the unchanging background of physical transformation. Therefore, the soul is infinite and beyond physical comparison. Evamatmanamatsthamaatmanevaamrusha prabho."
