ी से\nप्रार्थना की कि वे उन्हें अपना हृदय भगवान् हरि के चरणकमलों में स्थिर करने की और अपना\nप्राण छोड़ने की अनुमति दें। यह अनुमति देकर श्री शुकदेव उठ कर चले गये। तत्पश्चात् समस्त",
      "textEn": "The Absolute is distinct from me.\" In this way, while surrendering oneself to the Supreme Being, all those who are free from material\nafflictions, when that Takshak snake, with its full venom and teeth, reaches you\nand bites your foot, you will not even see. Neither will you see your dying body or\nyour surrounding world because you have already experienced yourself as separate from them\nwill be. Etatte kathitam tat, yadaatma prashnavannripa. What more can I do to explain the actions of the self-controlled? 13. Meaning of the word\n\nEtat—This; Ta—from you; Kathitam—said; Taat—Oh Parikshit; Yat—That; Atma—You; Pristavan—Asked; Nripa—Oh King; Hareh—Of God; Vishwa-atmanah—Of the soul of the universe; Chestham—Movements; Kim—What; Bhuyah—And further;\nShrotum—To listen; Ichchasi—You want. Oh, dear King Parikshit, I have narrated to you the stories of the Supreme Lord Hari of the universe—those\nAll the stories—which you had asked about at the beginning.\nWhat else do you want to hear? Meaning: While commenting on this verse, Srila Jiva Goswami, while quoting many verses from the Bhagavat,\nhas shown the high devotional state of King Parikshit, who was steadfast in his mind on Krishna,\nand was determined to return to the abode of the Lord. Thus, under the twelfth canto of Srimad Bhagavat, \"Maharaj Parikshit to Shukadeva\nGoswami's final teaching,\" the fifth chapter, composed by Srila Bhakti Vedanta Swami Prabhupada's\ndevout servants, is complete. Chapter six.\n\nThe death of Maharaj Parikshit.\n\nIn this chapter, the attainment of salvation by Maharaj Parikshit, the completion of the Yagya by Maharaj Janamejaya to kill all the serpents, the origin of the Vedas, and the division of Vedic literature by Srila Vedavyasa\nis described.\nAfter listening to the words of Shri Shukdev, Maharaj Parikshit said that after listening to the Bhagwat, which is the essence of the Puranas and is imbued with the nectar-like pastimes of the Supreme Lord,\nhe has attained the divine state of fearlessness\nand has become one with Brahma. Their ignorance has been removed, and by the grace of Shri Shukdev,\nthey have attained the supreme auspicious, tangible form of God, Lord Hari. As a result,\nall their fear of death has been removed. Thereafter, Shri Parikshit Maharaj prayed to Shukdev Goswami\nthat he should stabilize his heart in the lotus feet of Lord Hari and allow him to\ngive up his life. Giving this permission, Shri Shukdev got up and left. Thereafter, all"
